  "notes": "This change independently adapts evidence-resolution ordering and cite-or-abstain ideas from the supplied documents into a repository-native bounded candidate profile; no third-party code, source rows, or assets were copied. The helper is pure and performs no network, registry, store, claim-scope inference, evidence creation, policy evaluation, review, release, public projection, or publication. RESOLVED means only that caller-supplied synthetic references, bundle membership, current correction head, and canonical PolicyDecision projection agree. All other states fail closed, and non-resolved result objects retain no bundle identifier. Rollback is a normal revert of the feature commit; no live source, lifecycle, release, or published state is created."
